WEBVTT

00:00:03.400 --> 00:00:05.577
Here's Gem Island, the starter game.

00:00:05.583 --> 00:00:07.586
Let's make it pretty, without any code.

00:00:07.789 --> 00:00:08.973
First, a sea:

00:00:08.973 --> 00:00:12.056
in the 3D View's header, open the Add menu.

00:00:12.633 --> 00:00:13.905
Choose Mesh,

00:00:15.567 --> 00:00:16.699
then Plane.

00:00:18.067 --> 00:00:19.699
A small plane appears.

00:00:19.704 --> 00:00:22.311
Open the Add Plane panel at the bottom left:

00:00:22.351 --> 00:00:24.401
it adjusts what you just added.

00:00:24.967 --> 00:00:26.848
Set its Size to two hundred metres:

00:00:26.848 --> 00:00:28.607
water all around the island.

00:00:29.167 --> 00:00:31.686
And set its Z to minus zero point three,

00:00:31.686 --> 00:00:33.968
so the water sits just below the lawn.

00:00:34.533 --> 00:00:36.223
Now turn on Game in the header.

00:00:36.367 --> 00:00:38.062
The Scene view draws the level with the

00:00:38.062 --> 00:00:40.867
game's own renderer, as players will see it.

00:00:41.433 --> 00:00:44.382
The sky and sun come from GameStudio's sky kit,

00:00:44.382 --> 00:00:47.256
which has no panel, so ask Claude Code:

00:00:47.296 --> 00:00:49.601
a warm sunset with light fog.

00:00:49.688 --> 00:00:52.033
It switches the sky to its sunset preset

00:00:52.033 --> 00:00:54.970
with a lower sun, and turns on the world's mist,

00:00:54.970 --> 00:00:57.380
which the game draws as fog.

00:00:57.933 --> 00:01:00.261
There's the sunset, fading into the haze.

00:01:00.348 --> 00:01:02.003
Now turn the plane into water.

00:01:02.008 --> 00:01:04.685
In the Properties, open the Material tab

00:01:05.267 --> 00:01:06.539
and click New.

00:01:08.333 --> 00:01:10.301
Scroll down to the Game panel.

00:01:11.433 --> 00:01:12.698
It picks the game shader that

00:01:12.698 --> 00:01:14.574
draws this material in the game.

00:01:14.661 --> 00:01:16.559
Open the Game Shader menu.

00:01:17.133 --> 00:01:20.123
The library's thirty-three shaders come in groups.

00:01:20.163 --> 00:01:21.377
Open Water

00:01:22.400 --> 00:01:23.857
and choose Water.

00:01:24.900 --> 00:01:26.636
Scroll down to its settings.

00:01:27.400 --> 00:01:29.055
The defaults already look good.

00:01:29.060 --> 00:01:32.201
For an open sea, set Wave Length to fifteen metres.

00:01:32.767 --> 00:01:34.596
Now press F5 to play.

00:01:35.500 --> 00:01:37.422
Click Play on the title screen.

00:01:38.867 --> 00:01:40.208
There it is in the game:

00:01:40.214 --> 00:01:42.733
warm sunset light, haze in the distance,

00:01:42.733 --> 00:01:46.466
and waves rolling in around the island, all without code.

00:01:46.472 --> 00:01:48.544
Press F8 to stop.
